<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We employ the Price-to-Book \(P/B\) methodology as our primary valuation framework for ACB , as it better reflects the intrinsic value of net assets for banking institutions. The majority of a bank's assets \(primarily loans and investment securities\) and liabilities \(deposits, certificates of deposit\) are recorded at historical cost \(or discounted for credit risk provisions\). This metric also provides superior insight into loan portfolio risk, asset quality, and ROE profitability compared to the P/E approach, which exhibits greater volatility and sensitivity to macroeconomic factors such as interest rate cycles and economic conditions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
